{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3250","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3250","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3250\",\"parent_revision\":\"5d0fd6c158e4b919762a67aa826dcf8da407609b1a81c6b807f4439818a8a49b\",\"root_revision\":\"5d0fd6c158e4b919762a67aa826dcf8da407609b1a81c6b807f4439818a8a49b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n#3248 fixes plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md's missing explicit STATUS: DONE + SendMessage(to='team-lead', ...) completion-report instruction (it has the SendMessage tool grant but no instruction to use it for orchestrator notification, unlike technical-researcher.md:183 and fact-checker.md:107 which both have it).\\n\\nChecking sibling grooming-swarm agents for the same gap found it is not isolated to impact-analyst: plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md, plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md, and plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md all grant SendMessage but contain no explicit STATUS: DONE / SendMessage(to='team-lead', ...) instruction either (rtica-assessor happened to send a correct completion report during the observed run, but nothing in its prompt requires that \u2014 it is not a reliable contract for future runs).\\n\\nThis repo's own .claude/rules/agent-output-contracts.md already states the required pattern: \\\"When operating as a teammate (spawned via TeamCreate), also send: SendMessage(to='team-lead', summary='[brief]', message='[full STATUS block]')\\\" \u2014 and its Enforcement section explicitly calls out checking for this when writing or reviewing an agent file. The dh grooming-swarm agents appear to have been authored before this rule existed, or without checking against it.\\n\\nNot yet checked: every other dh:* agent under plugins/development-harness/agents/ that can be dispatched as a teammate (alignment-analyst.md is confirmed to have the same gap \u2014 verified directly, not just inferred from the pattern).\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 surfaced while grooming #3244; the impact-analyst gap fixed in #3248 turned out to be one instance of a wider pattern\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-27\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8ed05896efc4738127dec547f9ba8a3bc595fdadfb253dcf6cba0e7556e6ea18\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRBazrg\"}"}